<Base title="McQueen — Kartik Tagore" description="An RC car, an off-board model, and a phone network between them. Built with SRA.">
  <article class="paper-document">
      <a class="breadcrumb" href="/#work">← Back to the workbench</a>
      <header class="article-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Robotics · Python · PyTorch · Kotlin</p>
        <h1>McQueen</h1>
        <p class="lede">An RC car we turned autonomous. A camera on board, a model running elsewhere.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="prose">
        <figure class="photo">
          <img src="/img/mcqueen-car.png" width="480" height="295" alt="The red McQueen RC car with a camera rig mounted on top." decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>The car, with the camera rig bolted on.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>We put a camera and a Jetson on the car, but kept the model off-board. Frames go out over a mobile link; steering and throttle come back. The model was never the hard part. The loop was.</p>
        <LoopDiagram />
        <p>Everything interesting lived between the machines: a link that drops, a frame that arrives late, a command that's no longer useful by the time it lands. We worked on getting that pipeline running end to end on real hardware.</p>
        <p class="footnote">Built with SRA. The full account:<br /><a href="https://blog.sravjti.in/2026/10/20/mcqueen.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">McQueen: From Perception to Motion ↗</a></p>
      </div>
  </article>
</Base>
